## Tutorials

❮ Java Keywords

Thereturnkeyword finishes the execution of a method, and can be used to return a value from a method.

Tip:Use thevoidkeyword to specify that a method should not have a return value:

Read more about methods in ourJava Methods Tutorial.

❮ Java Keywords

### Code Examples

```
Example
A method with a return value:
public class Main {
  static
int
myMethod(int x) {
return
5 + x;
  }

  public static void main(String[] args) {
    System.out.println(myMethod(3));
  }
}
// Outputs 8 (5 + 3)
Try it Yourself »

---

Example
A method without any return values:
public class Main {
  static
void
myMethod() {
    System.out.println("I just got executed!");
  }

  public static void main(String[] args) {
    myMethod();
  }
}
Try it Yourself »
```

